# Vehicle Service Center UI Design (Amibica Auto)

Use these rules for **all** UI work in the vehicle service center workflow app. The app manages the full lifecycle from **Gate Entry to Delivery**. Prioritize **usability for workshop staff** over decorative visuals.

## Design principles

- **Minimal clutter** – Only show information needed for the current task.
- **Large touch targets** – Minimum 48dp for buttons and tappable areas (accessibility).
- **Clear status indicators** – Use colored status chips consistently.
- **Smooth visual hierarchy** – Section cards with clear headers; consistent spacing (e.g. 12–16dp).
- **Consistent spacing** – Use 8dp, 12dp, 16dp, 24dp; avoid one-off values.
- **Material3 design system** – Use MaterialTheme colors and typography; no hardcoded styles where theme tokens exist.
- **Soft elevation cards** – Default card elevation 2–4dp; rounded corners (12–20dp).
- **Rounded components** – Buttons, chips, text fields: 12–16dp corner radius.
- **Clean typography** – Prefer MaterialTheme.typography; ensure readable sizes (body ≥ 14sp).
- **Light neutral palette** – Backgrounds: near-white/light grey; accent colors only for status and primary actions.

## Status visualization (required)

Use these **status chip colors** everywhere (job status, part status, approval status):

| Status type   | Color   | Use for                          |
|---------------|---------|-----------------------------------|
| **Completed** | Green   | Done, approved, received, closed  |
| **Pending**   | Orange  | Awaiting action, estimate/insurance/billing pending |
| **On Hold**   | Red     | On hold, rejected, blocked       |
| **In Progress** | Blue   | In repair, in progress, ordered  |

Use `StatusChip` or equivalent from `ServiceCenterComponents` so colors stay consistent.

## Core UI patterns

### 1. Job List Screen

- **Job cards** must show: vehicle number, customer name, **job status badge**, **current repair stage**, **last update timestamp**.
- **Search bar** – Full-width, rounded; search by vehicle number, job card, customer.
- **Filter chips** – Status filters (e.g. All, Pending, In Progress, Completed); horizontal scroll if needed.
- **Branch filter** – Dropdown or chip to filter by branch (when user has multi-branch).
- **Pull to refresh** – Refresh job list from API/local source.

### 2. Job Detail Screen (modular section cards)

Use **section cards** with soft elevation and a clear header. Each section is a **card** (Overview, Documents, Insurance, Repair Progress, Parts, Billing, Gate Pass). Only show sections the **current role** can access (role-based visibility).

- **Overview card** – Vehicle details, customer details, job status.
- **Documents card** – List of required/uploaded documents; upload button.
- **Insurance card** – Survey details, approval status, notes.
- **Repair Progress card** – Stage timeline (vertical), progress photos.
- **Parts Tracking card** – Parts required list with status badges.
- **Billing card** – Insurance liability, customer payment, payment proof.
- **Gate Pass card** – Generate gate pass, delivery confirmation.

If a role cannot access a module (e.g. Billing), **do not show** that card at all; keep layout consistent (no empty placeholders for hidden modules).

### 3. Role-based visibility

- **StaffRole** (Gate Entry, Estimator, Insurance, Workshop, Parts, Billing, Manager, Admin) determines which Job Detail sections are visible.
- Map roles to sections (e.g. Billing role → Billing card; Workshop → Repair Progress; Insurance → Insurance card). Manager/Admin see all.
- Gracefully hide or omit unavailable modules; do not show disabled/greyed-out cards for “no access”.

### 4. Timeline view

- Repair stages must be shown as a **vertical timeline** with:
  - Icon or indicator per stage (e.g. circle with check for completed, dot for current).
  - Timestamp (or “In progress” / “Pending”) per stage.
- Use consistent spacing and connector lines between stages.

### 5. Photo upload UI

- **Progress photos**: display as **image grid** (e.g. 2–3 columns).
- **Camera/upload button** – Clearly visible (e.g. dashed border card with camera icon).
- **Preview modal** – Tap photo to open full-screen or modal preview; close button.

### 6. Dashboard Screen

- **Analytics cards** for:
  - Vehicles in workshop
  - Pending insurance approvals
  - Parts pending
  - Vehicles ready for delivery
- Use **simple charts or progress indicators** (e.g. LinearProgressIndicator, or small bar/count).
- Tapping a card can navigate to filtered Job List (e.g. “Pending insurance” → Jobs filtered by insurance pending).

### 7. Navigation

- **Bottom navigation** with exactly: **Dashboard**, **Jobs**, **Reports**, **Profile**.
- Keep labels and icons consistent; minimum 48dp touch target for nav items.

### 8. Accessibility

- **Readable typography** – Use MaterialTheme typography; avoid very small body text.
- **Sufficient contrast** – Prefer theme colors; status chips must have readable text on background.
- **Large buttons** – Minimum height 48dp for primary/secondary actions.

## Reference feel

- Similar to: **Uber Driver**, **Notion mobile**, **Linear**, **Stripe Dashboard mobile**.
- **Professional, production-ready**, suitable for staff using the app all day.

## Implementation notes

- Reuse `ServiceCenterComponents.kt` for: `StatusChip`, `SectionCard`, vertical timeline, photo grid + upload + preview modal.
- Use `JobStatus`, `RepairStage`, `PartStatus`, `ApprovalStatus` from `JobModels.kt` when mapping to status colors.
- Session/role from `DemoRepository.sessionFlow` (or equivalent) for role-based visibility in Job Detail.
